      "id": "android-forcible-process-termination",
      "observed": "On all four devices, both rounds pass 10 of 12 probes. Scripts that ignore SIGTERM survive destroy() followed by destroyForcibly() and the bounded wait. The timeout and output-limit probes fail; the tool correctly exits nonzero.",
      "sourceEvidence": "Installed Android SDK sources for API 28, 31 and 35 show Process.destroyForcibly() delegating to destroy(), and UNIXProcess not overriding it. This is consistent with the observed failure, not a separate syscall-level trace.",
      "sourceReference": "https://developer.android.com/reference/java/lang/Process#destroyForcibly()",
      "productionFollowup": "BunRuntimeService.ExecutionState uses the same Java method. Reproduce through the official plugin's Binder contract before claiming an official-payload failure, then implement an API-compatible, identity-safe forcible termination mechanism and add regression tests.",
      "disposition": "Do not lower minSdk or publish a patched experimental plugin before lifecycle gates are closed."
    }
